; ============================================================================
; cuBLASLt MARKER design, round 5 
 ; SPELLING-INDEPENDENT terms.
;
; Austin's standing doctrine: "we should never depend on the spelling of a
; node in the eclass." Operationalized:
;   1. Rules never bind NUMERIC values by destructuring class spellings 
;      terms carry POINTERS (site, layout tensors) and FINITE STRUCTURAL
;      CLASSIFICATIONS (operation, layout form) only.
;   2. Numeric facts a rule needs are read spelling-independently:
;      positional/structural access plus LATTICE BOUNDS (class-level
;      attributes shared by all spellings).
;   3. Extraction reads numerics as class-invariant facts (a literal the
;      whole class equals) or anchored at the elected enode's own
;      children; dead axes resolve by canonical choice at the reader.
;
; Round-4's CublasLtMatrixLayoutLit(order rows cols ld) is GONE: rows,
; cols, ld, m, n, k no longer exist in the egglog vocabulary at all. A
; descriptor reading is (site, layout tensor, layout FORM, operation) 
; the form is the finite classification that tells the EXTRACTOR how to
; compute the API numerics from the logical shape and (for static pitch)
; the elected layout term:
;   RightMajorContiguous : COL view = transpose; ld := storage cols
;   LeftMajorContiguous  : COL view = identity;  ld := storage rows
;   StaticRowPitch       : row-major with literal row pitch, unit inner
;                          stride; ld := the pitch entry's literal
;                          (dead row axis: canonical choice, see parser)
;
; The order sort is gone too: every reading is COL by convention (R9); a
; future ROW-convention family would be new FORM values, not numerics.
;
; Four fixed-arity contract constructors carry a final precision configuration.
; Lit dataflow arity stays a constant of the
; constructor name: base [a,b] / Bias [a,b,bias] / Accumulate [a,b,c] /
; AccumulateBias [a,b,c,bias].
; ============================================================================
(datatype CublasLtLogicalSite
  (CublasLtLogicalMatmulSite LogicalTensor LogicalTensor LogicalTensor))
;                            a             b             out
(datatype CublasLtOperation (CublasLtOperationN) (CublasLtOperationT))
; ROUND 8b (E1, re-attempted and LANDED): the layout-FORM child is
; DELETED. The round-8 refutation was WRONG: it tried to re-derive
; ORIENTATION from the layout term, which genuinely does not carry it at
; extent 1 — but orientation never had to come from the layout. It is
; already in the descriptor's OPERATION child, which the rules prove from
; the index map. Given the operation, the column-major view is fixed:
;   descriptor A: op=N -> (rows'=n, cols'=k)   op=T -> (rows'=k, cols'=n)
;   descriptor B: op=N -> (rows'=k, cols'=m)   op=T -> (rows'=m, cols'=k)
;   descriptor D:            (rows'=n, cols'=m)   [no transD]
; and for a contiguous layout the leading dimension IS the row count of
; that view (ld = rows'); a padded layout overrides it with its pitch.
; Form and operation were never independent: the two routes to op=T
; (a [n,k]-stored operand read right-major, a [k,n]-stored operand read
; left-major) yield the SAME ld, as do the two routes to op=N — so the
; operation is the child that survives. (ROUND 11: N/T live HERE, on the
; descriptor stratum, and nowhere above it — layouts, never logical
; transforms; the logical rules speak only in shapes.)
(datatype CublasLtOperandDescriptor
  (CublasLtOperandADescriptor
    CublasLtLogicalSite LayoutTensor CublasLtOperation)
  (CublasLtOperandBDescriptor
    CublasLtLogicalSite LayoutTensor CublasLtOperation))
; The D reading: the layout tensor is the op's CLAIMED output (moves
; under decoration). No operation child (transC/D not in scope).
(datatype CublasLtOutputDescriptor
  (CublasLtOutputDDescriptor
    CublasLtLogicalSite LayoutTensor))
; cublasLtEpilogue_t as a plain value enum (a FIELD, not a null slot).
(datatype CublasLtEpilogue
  (CublasLtEpilogueDefault)
  (CublasLtEpilogueRelu))
; ROUND 7 (E3): the dedicated static-pitch certificate relation is
; DELETED 
 ; the static reading arms match INJECTIVE strided layouts
; directly ((= (injectivity-of ?lt) (Injective)) + structure): for the
; unit-inner row-pitch shape, injectivity IS the ld clamp, and Ruling 1
; made symbolic pitches walkable. Injectivity still arrives by creator
; assertion (the padding rewrite in cublaslt_marker_desc.egg).
; Padding is entirely the bucketing ESTATE's business: the
; estate decides what to pad and to what pitch, mints the padded layout
; tensors, and asserts their injectivity. cuBLASLt only CONSUMES layout
; tensors + injectivity facts through its ordinary reading arms, so
; nothing here has to name the estate at all.
; --- THE four op constructors, one per runtime contract -------------------
; D = act(alpha * op(A)op(B))                       
 ; Lit [a, b]
(constructor LayoutTensorOpCublasLt
  (CublasLtLogicalSite
   CublasLtOperandDescriptor CublasLtOperandDescriptor
   CublasLtOutputDescriptor CublasLtEpilogue CublasLtConfig)
  LayoutTensorOp)
; D = act(alpha * op(A)op(B) + bias)                
 ; Lit [a, b, bias]
(constructor LayoutTensorOpCublasLtBias
  (CublasLtLogicalSite
   CublasLtOperandDescriptor CublasLtOperandDescriptor
   CublasLtOutputDescriptor LayoutTensor CublasLtEpilogue CublasLtConfig)
  LayoutTensorOp)
; D = act(alpha * op(A)op(B) + beta * C)            
 ; Lit [a, b, c]
(constructor LayoutTensorOpCublasLtAccumulate
  (CublasLtLogicalSite
   CublasLtOperandDescriptor CublasLtOperandDescriptor
   CublasLtOutputDescriptor LayoutTensor CublasLtEpilogue CublasLtConfig)
  LayoutTensorOp)
; D = act(alpha * op(A)op(B) + beta * C + bias)     
 ; Lit [a, b, c, bias]
(constructor LayoutTensorOpCublasLtAccumulateBias
  (CublasLtLogicalSite
   CublasLtOperandDescriptor CublasLtOperandDescriptor
   CublasLtOutputDescriptor LayoutTensor LayoutTensor CublasLtEpilogue CublasLtConfig)
  LayoutTensorOp)
; ============================================================================
